echose:mo,efflux:ho,mitotic:go,oppilation:_o,binnacle:vo,espial:yo,innermostly:bo,parabola:xo,appoggiatura:So,zomboruk:Co,introspective:wo,"jinny road":`An inclined road in a coal mine, on which loaded cars descend by gravity, drawing up empty ones. Knight.`,plebeianism:To,excentricity:Eo,viperine:Do,caliber:Oo,calyon:ko,exsudation:Ao,interosseous:jo,plumule:Mo,welew:No,moppet:Po,informous:Fo,levelly:Io,multinodate:Lo,octamerous:Ro,alopecy:zo,"worldly-minded":`Devoted to worldly interests; mindful of the affairs of the present life, and forgetful of those of the future; loving and pursuing this world's goods, to the exclusion of piety and attention to spiritual concerns. -- World"ly*mind\`ed*ness, n.`,megasthenic:Bo,skyed:Vo,binuclear:Ho,prenomination:Uo,parietary:Wo,pacable:Go,telethermograph:Ko,haemochrome:qo,returner:Jo,placoides:Yo,gnarled:Xo,semiadherent:Zo,polemist:Qo,hispanicize:$o,micropegmatite:es,telangiectasy:ts,popularly:ns,launce:rs,caries:is,notum:as,cupulate:os,alan:ss,aliferous:cs,recumbency:ls,snobbism:us,unpractical:ds,electron:fs,"weather signal":`Any signal giving information about the weather. The system used by the United States Weather Bureau includes temperature, cold or hot wave, rain or snow, wind direction, storm, and hurricane signals.`,lentoid:ps,compliancy:ms,discursion:hs,scalloping:gs,"in transitu":`In transit; during passage; as, goods in transitu.`,disfavorable:_s,omnifarious:vs,carbonide:ys,crenelled:bs,hone:xs,hematocele:Ss,marketable:Cs,plaudit:ws,saturnism:Ts,secularness:Es,twelfthtide:Ds,competence:Os,alienable:ks,parochialize:As,calyptriform:js,staidness:Ms,synonyme:Ns,irreconcilability:Ps,dressmaking:Fs,commutability:Is,anchoress:Ls,conventionalism:Rs,engager:zs,"vapor tension":`The pressure or tension of a confined body of vapor. The pressure of a given saturated vapor is a function of the temperature only, and may be measured by introducing a small quantity of the substance into a barometer and noting the depression of the column of mercury.`,delight:Bs,beryl:Vs,campaign:Hs,"nudum pactum":`A bare, naked contract, without any consideration. Tomlins.`,dynamitism:Us,escaloped:Ws,"grass-grown":`Overgrown with grass; as, a grass-grown road.`,seminifical:Gs,craterous:Ks,helminthology:qs,steinbock:Js,thoughtful:Ys,itchy:Xs,subbrachial:Zs,fonly:Qs,echinoid:$s,isagelous:ec,slobberer:tc,roarer:nc,columbella:rc,viola:ic,"knight service":`A tenure of lands held by knights on condition of performing military service. See Chivalry, n., 4. KNIGHT SERVICE; KNIGHT'S SERVICE Knight service. Also Knight's service. 1.  (Feud. Law) The military service by rendering which a knight held his lands; also, the tenure of lands held on condition of performing military service. By far the greater part of England [in the 13th century] is held of the king by knight's service. . . . In order to understand this tenure we must form the conception of a unit of military service. That unit seems to be the service of one knight or fully armed horseman (servitium unius militis) to be done to the king in his army for forty days in the year, if it be called for. . . . The limit of forty days seems to have existed rather in theory than practice. Pollock & Mait. 2.  Service such as a knight can or should render; hence, good or valuable service. KNIGHT'S FEE Knight's fee. (Feudal Law)  The fee of a knight; specif., the amount of land the holding of which imposed the obligation of knight service, being sometimes a hide or less, sometimes six or more hides.`,cultivable:ac,heraldship:oc,illegalize:sc,nude:cc,plunder:lc,fricative:uc,lamprel:dc,negotious:fc,marsipobranchia:pc,"-oid":`A suffix or combining form meaning like, resembling, in the form of; as in anthropoid, asteroid, spheroid.`,maked:mc,rhinoscope:hc,greengrocer:gc,headboard:_c,ascendable:vc,shopwoman:yc,sagene:bc,ensilage:xc,amole:Sc,"auction pitch":`A game of cards in which the players bid for the privilege of determining or "pitching" the trump suit.  R. F. Foster.`,a